t_encoding\": \"utf-8\",\n        \"size_bytes\": 3518,\n        \"source\": \"23dc82206dd5f18fdc4524f55ad48286b63f5820:charness-artifacts/probe/2026-09-15-v8.7.1-release-observer.json\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"carrier_path\": \"charness-artifacts/critique/workers/review-20260915T130702Z-3593657/semantic-input/0001-content.bin\",\n        \"carrier_sha256\": \"e0635efaae7cd07fe0af584025992d3a2f120706adff05a4069acf75eee904e1\",\n        \"content_sha256\": \"e0635efaae7cd07fe0af584025992d3a2f120706adff05a4069acf75eee904e1\",\n        \"disposition\": \"present\",\n        \"path\": \"charness-artifacts/release-review/2026-09-15-v8.7.1-claims.md\",\n        \"prompt_content\": \"# v8.7.1 claims review (parent narrative, second prepare)\\n\\nDate: 2026-09-15. Reviewer: parent agent (prepared the release lane).\\nObserver: distinct read-only subagent (`v871-claims-review-2`), verdict PASS.\\n\\nThis is a fresh review: the first prepare's line could not resume after a\\nreviewer-demanded code repair landed on top of it, so the line was\\nrecovered (backup ref `backup-871-release-attempt1`, reset to pre-prepare,\\ncontent replayed) and prepared anew. This narrative binds the NEW prepared\\ncommit `34e767973e60fff9fcadf054e165085356e44f6b` only.\\n\\n## What was audited\\n\\nThe prepared record `charness-artifacts/release/latest.md` at `34e767973` —\\nits assertions only, not code correctness (covered by the release critique\\nworker and the standing suite).\\n\\n## Observer findings (all hold)\\n\\n1. Previous 8.7.0 in pre-bump manifests; target 8.7.1 on every versioned\\n   surface (3 version lines in packaging, 2 in marketplace).\\n2. Tag `v8.7.1` absent locally and on origin; latest published tag `v8.7.0`.\\n3. Branch `main`, remote `origin`.\\n4. No-drift report matches an independent `current_release.py` re-run\\n   exactly (4 versioned + 1 presence-only).\\n5. Fresh-checkout probe set matches the declared set.\\n6. Critique artifact exists and is tracked.\\n7.